abstract: >
  Software supporting a comparative study of three-dimensional super-resolution
  for segmented porous nickel-manganese-cobalt oxide (NMC) microstructures.
  The study compares bicubic interpolation with four deep-learning architectures:
  SRCNN, SRResNet, SRGAN, and SRUNet, at scaling factors of 2, 4, and 8.
  The workflow uses virtual microstructures generated by a stochastic model
  and evaluates reconstructions using image-quality, voxel-wise, interface,
  and transport-related metrics, including geodesic and effective tortuosity.

keywords:
  - "3D super-resolution"
  - "porous microstructures"
  - "NMC cathodes"
  - "deep learning"
  - "SRCNN"
  - "SRResNet"
  - "SRGAN"
  - "SRUNet"
  - "stochastic microstructure modeling"
  - "geodesic tortuosity"
  - "effective tortuosity"
  - "battery imaging"

